---
import InstallTabs from "./InstallTabs.astro";
---

<section class="py-16 sm:py-24">
  <div id="install" class="anchor-offset container-app">
    <div>
      <span class="pill">▸ install</span>
      <h2 class="heading mt-3 text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-4xl">
        Build Yaran for your <span class="text-[color:var(--color-accent)]">workspace.</span>
      </h2>
      <p class="mt-3 text-[color:var(--color-muted)]">
        Start from the source repository. No separate server package is needed:
        <code>yaran</code> opens the terminal UI and <code>yaran server</code> serves
        the browser UI from the same binary.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="mt-6 grid items-stretch gap-4 md:grid-cols-2">
      <div class="min-w-0"><InstallTabs /></div>
      <div class="card p-6 text-sm text-[color:var(--color-muted)]">
        <h3 class="heading text-base font-semibold text-[color:var(--color-text)]">From this fork</h3>
        <p class="mt-3">
          Building requires Rust and Node.js/npm. Running Yaran requires Git and
          the agent CLIs you choose. The GitHub CLI is optional for pull-request features.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3">
          Source and release history live in{" "}
          <a href="https://github.com/SiavZ/dux-amq-setup" class="text-[color:var(--color-accent)] hover:underline">SiavZ/dux-amq-setup</a>.
          No Yaran website domain, Homebrew tap, or npm publication is claimed here.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3">
          Historical{" "}
          <a href="https://github.com/patrickdappollonio/dux/releases" class="text-[color:var(--color-accent)] hover:underline">upstream dux releases</a>,{" "}
          <a href="https://github.com/patrickdappollonio/homebrew-tap" class="text-[color:var(--color-accent)] hover:underline">Homebrew tap</a>, and{" "}
          <a href="https://www.npmjs.com/package/@patrickdappollonio/dux" class="text-[color:var(--color-accent)] hover:underline">npm package</a>{" "}
          belong to dux, not this Yaran fork.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
